silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_05_glue_as_kleisli_arrow_concrete_anchor_1 a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "GlueKleisliAnchorTypedLegRecordExample" .
silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_05_glue_as_kleisli_arrow_concrete_anchor_1 silm:hasExample "In 'GlueKleisliAnchorTypedLegRecord', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, TypedLeg_record represents the olog object VetRecord77 (the veterinary examination record for Mittens from 2024) as a typed colimit leg. The glue arrow lambda_rec: TypedLeg_record -> Mittens is one of the ten cocone legs that must be present and compatible for glue to produce the Mittens colimit apex.." .
